so how about all that Call of Duty  advanced warfare multiplayer footage huh  look at these dudes it's jetting through  the air every which way it's crazy  getting up on rooftops flying through  windows turning invisible to sneak up on  fools spotting their glowing silhouettes  through walls climbing into like a big  mech suit huh does this remind any lots  of titanfall like a lot  yes you'd certainly be forgiven for  thinking that sledgehammers new entry in  the Call of Duty series bears strong  similarities to respawns high-flying  parkour fueled shooter there always was  a kinship there perhaps due to the fact  that the guys who launched us into the  modern warfare era went on to make  titanfall the speed of the action the  feel of the weapons the fragility of  your soldier the influence of call of  duty on titanfall has always been  apparent but titanfall distinguished  itself with its eponymous Titans and  with jump jet fueled while running  antics the latter created a whole new  spectrum of mobility which led to new  tactics new threats and a newly  invigorated multiplayer experience it  felt substantially different than call  of duty now along comes advanced warfare  with its own game-changing antics and  it's hard not to wonder just how much  overlap there is in advanced warfare  your exosuit enables seven different  abilities as far as we know and four of  them line up almost exactly with  titanfall advanced warfare has a cloak  ability titanfall has a cloak ability  advanced warfare has a see dude through  walls ability titanfall has a see dudes  through walls ability advanced warfare  has a boost health ability and a boost  speed ability titanfall has an ability  that does both advanced warfare has a  hulking mech suit with a big honkin gun  titanfall has well Titans okay that's  not really good parallel but when it  comes to the EXO abilities there is some  significant common ground even more  significant are the movement abilities  both games allow players to double jump  which results in a lot of roof hopping  and windowentry you can strike from a  wider variety of places in any given  environment so you must consider a  broader spectrum of offensive and  defensive strategies furthermore in  advanced warfare you can hover midair to  mess with where your opponent expects  you to be in titanfall you can wall hang  and accomplish the same thing a lot of  the tactical complexity that titanfall  introduced with its movement abilities  is present in Call of Duty advanced  warfare but there's one key difference  the boost dodge vs the wall run a boost  dodge in advanced warfare is a quick  dash you can execute at any time to  strafe quickly out of the way or change  direction sharply  in midair while running in titanfall is  a traversal tool dependent on a flat  vertical surface allowing you to  speedily cover distance and reach new  areas a boost dodge is a sharp staccato  beat wall running is a smooth legato  phrase the difference is crucial and it  sets the tone for to significantly  different play experiences the boost  dodge quickens the already fast call of  duty pace speeding up the tempo so that  seconds matter more than ever before  your target could be there one instant  gone the next your enemy could be across  the room now but in your face by the  time you aim down sights the boost dodge  ratchets up the intensity of evasion and  engagement but advanced warfare still  requires the same skills Call of Duty  has always demanded speed precision  awareness of your foe your weapons and  your environment titanfall on the other  hand demanded a new skill in order to  wall run successfully you couldn't just  know where the walls were you needed to  know their contours set your angles of  approach manage your momentum and know  where you're going next it can be a  smoother more prolonged maneuver so your  strategy has to include more potential  movements while running makes titanfall  combat feel more cohesive for a moment  to moment because you need to chain  together multiple actions to excel the  result being that though these two games  may have some striking similarities they  actually play very differently boost  dodging feels like exploiting the space  you're in wall running feels like  coexisting with your environment in Call  of Duty you feel like a visitor to the  places where you wage war in titanfall  you have to make them your home now if  it sounds like I'm favoring titanfall  here it's just because I have more  experience with it I had an absolute  blast playing advanced warfare  multiplayer matches and the kinetic  freedom of the double jump and the boost  dodge really feel like they have the  potential to reinvent Call of Duty  multiplayer in a more profound way than  we've seen in a long time personally I'm  excited but what about you does all this  mobility stuff sound cool or are you  worried about how it will change the  core gameplay join the discussion in the  comments below and be sure to check out  GameSpot's other video features on the  first reveal of advanced warfare  multiplayer action  you
 

